  "created": "2026-08-19T06:45:37.55Z",
  "description": "A lightweight, zero-dependency WebSocket library for .NET, implementing RFC 6455 from the ground up using raw TcpListener/TcpClient. Supports both server-side and client-side WebSocket connections.",
  "iconFile": "logo.png",
  "id": "LHZ.WebSocket",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-19T06:48:42.583Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "iQ0oxyx1+1pKhGq0U9aFb0LG8/Xia2GicI1fx44Ppp7Ido3lvF1b9/hvak1GMsRstbjQGz/uPYCudE6MIn+ehA==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 153789,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/lhzcm/LHZ.WebSocket",
  "published": "2026-08-19T06:45:37.55Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.1:\n- Fix: handshake handling is now concurrent, a slow client no longer blocks the accept loop\n- Fix: client-role connections now mask every outgoing frame (RFC 6455 §5.1), with a cryptographic masking key\n- Fix: the client collection is now per server instance instead of static\n- Fix: OnClientClose event subscription no longer leaks\n- Fix: masking no longer mutates the caller's buffer\n- Fix: client handshake can parse restricted response headers (e.g. Connection)\n- Add: server-side handshake validation (Sec-WebSocket-Key / Sec-WebSocket-Version 13) with HTTP 400 rejection\n- Add: automatic Close frame reply on receiving a Close frame\n- Add: fragmentation validation (reject orphan Continuation frames, control frames are never merged into messages)\n- Add: 10 interop tests (client-server round trip, masking, concurrent handshakes, handshake validation, close reply, fragmentation)",
